  ('stowe-vermont', '12A', 'Stowe', 'United States', 'Vermont''s highest peak, the East''s toughest four runs, and', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'New England', '{"ski","romance","culinary","family","adventure","entertainment","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Stowe = Vail Resorts / Epic (acquired Feb 2017); on MOUNT MANSFIELD (Vermont''s highest peak, 4,395 ft) + Spruce Peak, linked by the Over Easy gondola; lift-served summit ~3,700 ft, base ~1,559 ft, ~2,360 ft vertical","485 acres, 116 trails, ~12 lifts (2 gondolas); the legendary ''FRONT FOUR'' (Goat, Starr, National, Liftline) - among the toughest lift-served runs in the East; longest run Toll Road 4.3 mi; ~224 in snow + 83% snowmaking; no night skiing; 4 terrain parks","RESORT vs TOWN: the classic town of Stowe (''the Ski Capital of the East'') is ~7 mi away via the VT-108 Mountain Road - it holds the village (church steeple, covered bridges), inns + the Trapp Family Lodge","Lodge at Spruce Peak = marquee slope-side luxury (self-described ''4-diamond'', full spa); Trapp Family Lodge (Sound-of-Music von Trapps) = Austrian-style 2,600-ac estate IN THE TOWN (not the resort) with premier Nordic (167 km) + von Trapp Brewing","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: marquee Eastern resort but Vail reports visitation only in aggregate - no per-resort count published - consensus only","BTV ~45 min / ~35 mi (verify); Boston ~3.5 hr, Montreal ~2-2.5 hr, NYC ~5-6 hr drive; a marquee FALL-FOLIAGE town (second major season, late Sep-mid Oct)","NO on-site cat/heli (fully lift-served; Mansfield backcountry - Bruce/Teardrop trails - is self-guided/separate); NO natural hot springs (none on Mansfield/at Stowe); NO avalanche center (low-avalanche Eastern terrain - Mt Washington Avalanche Center is a different NH mountain)","Altitude LOW (no AMS factor); winter spine = Eastern ice/hardpack + extreme cold/wind chill on Mansfield + VT-108 Mountain Road winter driving (Smugglers'' Notch VT-108 closed Nov-Apr); Epic/lift prices dynamic; Vail sites erroring at build time (verify)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"Copley Hospital, 528 Washington Highway, Morrisville (~10 mi) - community hospital, 24/7 emergency services; higher-level trauma to UVM Medical Center, Burlington (~45 min)","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"NO AVALANCHE CENTER governs Stowe (low-avalanche, patrolled, lift-served Eastern terrain - do NOT cite CAIC/UAC/BTAC/GNFAC; the Mt Washington Avalanche Center covers a DIFFERENT mountain in New Hampshire, not Stowe); ALTITUDE is LOW (Mansfield 4,395 ft - AMS not a factor); the winter spine is ICE/HARDPACK (''Eastern ice'' - sharp edges, ski in control, pronounced on the Front Four), extreme COLD + WIND CHILL on exposed Mount Mansfield (frostbite/hypothermia - layer, cover skin, warm-up breaks), and VERMONT WINTER DRIVING (VT-108 Mountain Road steep/winding; Smugglers'' Notch VT-108 closed Nov-Apr; winter tires/chains, check VTrans 511vt.com); self-guided Mansfield backcountry (Bruce/Teardrop) unpatrolled; tree-wells in glades"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY, MLK, Presidents'' Week, mid-winter weekends) + a big fall-foliage peak (late Sep-mid Oct)","shoulder":"early Dec (pre-holiday) + late-Mar/April spring skiing","green":"mud season (Apr-May) + Nov pre-snow; summer (golf, concerts, Rec Path) is a genuine third season, not a true low","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + Lodge at Spruce Peak 3-6 mo (holidays + peak foliage longer); regular winter 2-4 mo; Epic by early fall","off_season_specials":"fall foliage; spring skiing; summer village + golf + Rec Path + Trapp Nordic/brewery; midweek value","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'', spring break; peak fall foliage (Oct); Stowe Derby ski race (dates/route verify)","campaign_start":"FIRE late-summer (Jul-Sep) foliage pre-book + Epic r