  ('telluride-colorado', '12A', 'Telluride', 'United States', 'A Victorian box-canyon town, a free gondola to Mountain', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Mountain West', '{"ski","adventure","wellness","culinary","entertainment","romance","family"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Telluride = Telski (independent, Epic Pass partner - most full Epic tiers include 7 days); a genuine 1880s Victorian box-canyon mining town (National Historic Landmark, 8,754 ft) + modern Mountain Village (~9,545 ft)","FREE public pedestrian gondola links town and Mountain Village (opened Dec 1996, ~13 min, cresting ~10,540 ft) - a rare free town-to-base lift + ski access","One of the biggest verticals in the US: 4,425 ft total (base 8,725 / summit 13,150; lift-served 3,845 ft); 2,000+ acres; 127 trails; 2 gondolas + 12 chairlifts; terrain ~23 beg/36 int/41 adv; no night skiing","Steep hike-to: Palmyra Peak (~13,320 ft), Gold Hill Chutes, Black Iron Bowl; ~280-330 in snowfall (range)","REAL heli-skiing: Telluride Helitrax (since 1982, ~200 sq mi San Juan terrain, based at The Peaks) - Colorado''s ORIGINAL/most-experienced heli op, NOT the only one (Silverton also flies); NO confirmed Telluride cat operation","Ultra bed base: Madeline Hotel & Residences (Auberge), The Peaks Resort & Spa (Colorado''s largest spa), Lumiere (Dunton), historic-town New Sheridan (1895); Allred''s fine dining atop the gondola (10,551 ft)","Remote/high-spend: MTJ ~65 mi (main jet), TEX ~6 mi (small/weather-dependent), DEN ~330 mi (~6-7 hr); festival town (Bluegrass Jun, Film Festival Sep)","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: high-spend, lower-volume, remote by consensus - never hard-state a number; CAIC ''Northern San Juan'' zone; Telluride Medical Center (Level V trauma, region''s only 24/7, air-evac transfers); season 2025-26 27 Nov-5 Apr; NO developed natural hot springs (Ouray/Orvis ~50 mi)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); a